Thanks for porting this from the Linux dwmac-style K1 EMAC driver.

A few questions on the new drivers/net/spacemit/k1_emac.c:

- K1_DLINE_MAX_CODE is defined as "(FIELD_MAX(K1_APMU_TX_DLINE_CODE) - 1)".
  Is the "-1" intentional (reserving the max code value), or is this meant
  to just be FIELD_MAX(...)? A short comment explaining why one less than
  the field's max is used for the delay line would help future maintainers.

- The descriptor structures (struct k1_emac_desc) are plain u32 fields
  written/read directly without any readl/writel or endian-conversion
  helpers visible in this hunk - can you confirm these descriptors are
  accessed through proper I/O accessors (and barriers/cache
  flush/invalidate for ARCH_DMA_MINALIGN-aligned DMA buffers) elsewhere in
  the file, given this is a DMA-coherent-by-convention ring buffer design?

- K1_TX_DESC_COUNT is 4 while K1_RX_DESC_COUNT is 16 - is that asymmetry
  deliberate (matching the Linux driver), or just a smaller TX ring for
  u-boot's typically short TFTP/NFS bursts?

- Link: tag points to a Linux lore thread, not a kernel commit; have the
  register definitions and timing constants (K1_TX_TIMEOUT_MS,
  K1_MDIO_TIMEOUT_MS) been validated against real K1 hardware rather than
  just transcribed from the Linux driver?
